## One deviation, stated exactly

`dao.data.md`'s `:stream` rule says the `:opaque` fallback "defends against a malformed **or throwing** third-party implementation of the protocol." I implemented the malformed case (non-`:dao.stream/ok` outcome → `:opaque` node, tested). Defending against a *throwing* implementation requires a catch that is portable across CLJ/CLJS/CLJD — the project's house idiom is `(catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _)` (e.g. `dao/stream/ws.cljc:89`) — which uses reader conditionals, directly forbidden by the doc's own "No reader conditionals / nothing host-specific" constraint (restated in the task). There is no conditional-free catch that is correct on all three hosts (`:default` fails CLJ; `Throwable` is unresolved in CLJS). So a throwing descriptor propagates today. Fix is one `try` + the house idiom in `stream-node` if the doc owner relaxes that constraint — the doc should pick one: either the throw defense or the no-reader-conditionals rule, they can't both hold.

Everything else is exactly per the frozen spec — the doc held up as a complete implementation contract.
